<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to auction 4.2 bln pesos of Cetes.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to auction 4.2 bln pesos of Cetes.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mixico said it would auction 4.2 billion pesos worth of Cetes at its primary auction on Tuesday next week.</p>
<p>This represents an increase of 600 million pesos from last week's auction when 3.6 billion pesos were on offer.  </p>
<p>The central bank said it will also auction 500 million pesos of Bondes and 550 million UDIs of UDI bonos.</p>
<p>CETES</p>
<p>    Terms	  Amount	   Fixed rates:</p>
<p>    28  days     800 million pesos  18.44 pct</p>
<p>    90  days     1.2 bln pesos  18.70 pct</p>
<p>    182 days     1.2 bln pesos  18.80 pct</p>
<p>    343 days     1.0 bln pesos  17.36 pct</p>
<p>BONDES</p>
<p>    728 days     500 million pesos  100.000</p>
<p>UDIBONOS</p>
<p>    1,078 days   200 million UDIs   100.38027</p>
<p>    1,806 days   350 million UDIs   100.58173</p>
<p>((-- Caroline Brothers, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7902))</p>
